<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <%- include('_head', { graph, pageTitle }) %>
</head>
<body class="cc-task-body">
  <main class="cc-task">
    <nav class="cc-task-nav">
      <a class="cc-link" href="/hivenues/studio/<%= graph.identity.slug %>">Back to Studio</a>
      <span class="cc-draft-status">Working Version <%= revision %></span>
    </nav>
    <p class="cc-kicker">Guided site shaping</p>
    <h1>Shape the public story and its composition.</h1>
    <p class="cc-task__dek">The three text fields below are visitor-facing copy, not private design notes. Direction changes the structural composition around the same canonical draft. Nothing becomes visitor-facing until you explicitly release the website.</p>

    <div class="cc-setup-grid">
      <form class="cc-setup-form" method="post" action="/hivenues/studio/<%= graph.identity.slug %>/setup">
        <input type="hidden" name="expectedRevision" value="<%= revision %>">
        <input type="hidden" name="expectedDraftDigest" value="<%= draftDigest %>">
        <div class="cc-field">
          <label for="cc-purpose">1 · Why this place exists</label>
          <textarea id="cc-purpose" name="purpose" required><%= graph.intent.purpose %></textarea>
          <small>Public story copy. Tell visitors what the place is for in ordinary language.</small>
        </div>
        <div class="cc-field">
          <label for="cc-material">2 · Visitor-facing story / atmosphere</label>
          <textarea id="cc-material" name="presenceMaterial" required><%= graph.intent.presenceMaterial %></textarea>
          <small>This appears on the public site. Describe the real place and atmosphere; do not put internal art-direction instructions here.</small>
        </div>
        <fieldset class="cc-field" style="border:0;padding:0">
          <legend>3 · Direction</legend>
          <div class="cc-choice-grid">
            <label class="cc-choice">
              <input type="radio" name="direction" value="poster" <%= graph.intent.direction === 'poster' ? 'checked' : '' %>>
              <strong>Poster room</strong>
              <span>Dense, tactile, event-led, nocturnal.</span>
            </label>
            <label class="cc-choice">
              <input type="radio" name="direction" value="editorial" <%= graph.intent.direction === 'editorial' ? 'checked' : '' %>>
              <strong>Editorial field notes</strong>
              <span>Open, publication-like, media-led, quiet.</span>
            </label>
            <label class="cc-choice">
              <input type="radio" name="direction" value="hospitality" <%= graph.intent.direction === 'hospitality' ? 'checked' : '' %>>
              <strong>Hospitality table</strong>
              <span>Image-led, menu-forward, warm, service-aware.</span>
            </label>
          </div>
        </fieldset>
        <div class="cc-field">
          <label for="cc-participation">4 · Visitor invitation</label>
          <textarea id="cc-participation" name="participation" required><%= graph.intent.participation %></textarea>
          <small>Public copy describing useful next steps. The underlying mechanics remain truthful and separate.</small>
        </div>
        <button class="cc-button cc-button--ink" type="submit">Save story & direction to draft</button>
      </form>

      <section class="cc-direction-preview" aria-label="Current generated first draft">
        <% if (family.id === 'poster') { %>
          <%- include('compositions/poster-canvas', { graph, media, heroMedia, logoMedia, contact, primaryActivity, oob: false }) %>
        <% } else if (family.id === 'editorial') { %>
          <%- include('compositions/editorial-canvas', { graph, media, heroMedia, logoMedia, contact, primaryActivity, oob: false }) %>
        <% } else { %>
          <%- include('compositions/hospitality-canvas', { graph, media, heroMedia, logoMedia, contact, primaryActivity, oob: false }) %>
        <% } %>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
  <script src="/htmx/htmx.min.js" defer></script>
</body>
</html>
